module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.EtaleCohomology.BrauerGroupScheme.AlgebraSheaf
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.FreeSheafification
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.InternalEndPoints

/-!
# The endomorphism algebra of a finite free sheaf of modules is determined by its points

Let `S` be a scheme and let `I` be a finite type. The endomorphism algebra sheaf
`End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` of the free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules on `I` is the internal hom
`𝒪_S^{(I)} ⟶[·] 𝒪_S^{(I)}`, and `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.curryHomEquiv'` identifies its
*points* — the morphisms `𝒪_S ⟶ End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` — with the endomorphisms of `𝒪_S^{(I)}`. This
file proves that a morphism *out of* `End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` is determined by its composites with those
points. Consequently the map on endomorphisms induced by a morphism of algebra sheaves
(`CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.pointMap`) determines the morphism itself, which is the
injectivity [Stacks, Tag 0A2K] needs in order to recover a morphism of algebra sheaves from its
action on endomorphisms.

The mechanism is a *finite dual basis*, and it is formulated for an arbitrary monoidal closed
preadditive category. Suppose `F` carries points `e i : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F` and coordinates
`p i : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C`, indexed by a finite type, with `∑ i, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F`. Then the internal hom
`F ⟶[C] Y` is the `I`-fold biproduct of `Y`: the morphisms
`ihomCoord (e i) Y : (F ⟶[C] Y) ⟶ Y` and `ihomIncl (p i) Y : Y ⟶ (F ⟶[C] Y)` satisfy
`ihomIncl (p i) Y ≫ ihomCoord (e j) Y = δ_{ij}` and
`∑ i, ihomCoord (e i) Y ≫ ihomIncl (p i) Y = 𝟙`. So a morphism out of `F ⟶[C] Y` is determined
by its composites with the `ihomIncl (p i) Y`, and when `Y` too is generated by its points those
composites are in turn determined by the points of `F ⟶[C] Y`.

A free sheaf of modules on a finite index type has such a dual basis: the points are Mathlib's
`SheafOfModules.ιFree` and the coordinates are built from the universal property of
`SheafOfModules.free I` as a coproduct of copies of `𝒪_S`. The same data also exhibits
`End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` as the free sheaf of modules on `I × I`, which is the system of matrix units of
the matrix algebra.

## Main definitions

* `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.ihomCoord` and `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.ihomIncl`: the
  coordinate and the inclusion of an internal hom attached to a point, respectively a coordinate,
  of the source.
* `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.ihomIsoOfDualBasis`: an object with a matching family of points
  indexed by `ι × ι` is the internal endomorphism object of an object with a dual basis indexed
  by `ι`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.freeModule`, `freeInj` and `freeProj`: the free sheaf of
  `𝒪_S`-modules on a type, its tautological points, and its coordinates.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.freeProdToEndAlgebra`: the comparison
  `𝒪_S^{(I × I)} ⟶ End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` carrying the generator indexed by `(i, j)` to the elementary
  endomorphism which reads off the `i`-th coordinate and writes it in the `j`-th place.

## Main results

* `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.sum_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl`: **a finite dual basis of `F`
  splits the internal hom out of `F` into its coordinates.**
* `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.hom_ext_of_dualBasis` and
  `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.hom_ext_of_curry'`: **morphisms out of an internal hom
  `F ⟶[C] Y` are determined by their composites with the coordinate inclusions**, and — when `Y`
  is generated by its points — by their composites with the points of `F ⟶[C] Y`.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.sum_freeProj_comp_freeInj`: the tautological points and
  coordinates are a dual basis of a finite free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext`,
  `endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext'` and
  `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.eq_of_pointMap_eq`: **a morphism out of `End(𝒪_S^{(I)})`
  is determined by its values on the points**, for a finite index type `I`; in particular a
  morphism of sheaves of algebras `End(𝒪_S^{(I)}) ⟶ End(E)` is determined by the map it induces
  on endomorphisms.
* `Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme.freeProdIsoEndAlgebra` and
  `nonempty_iso_freeProd_endAlgebra`: **`End(𝒪_S^{(I)}) ≅ 𝒪_S^{(I × I)}`** as sheaves of
  modules, so the endomorphism algebra of a finite free sheaf of modules is again a finite free
  sheaf of modules.

## Implementation notes

**No duality theory is used.** What `CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.ihomDualHom` gives from an
`ExactPairing (𝒪_S^{(I)}) D` is an identification of `End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` with `𝒪_S^{(I)} ⊗ D`, and
that is of no use until `D` is known to be free — which is the self-duality of a finite free
sheaf of modules, and this library does not have it. The matrix units `ihomIncl` and `ihomCoord`
are available directly from the description of `SheafOfModules.free I` as a coproduct of copies
of the unit, they need no pairing, and they prove the stronger statement: `End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` is
itself free.

**Why every scheme-level proof is term-mode.** The ring sheaf the tensor product of sheaves of
`𝒪_S`-modules is formed over is `Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf`, and
`S.sheaf : TopCat.Sheaf CommRingCat S` fits its argument only after unfolding `TopCat.Sheaf`.
That unfolding is unavailable at the `implicit` transparency `rw` and `simp` match at, so a
`rw` whose pattern is present is nevertheless rejected on a goal mentioning `freeModule S I`.
Every rewrite therefore happens in the abstract section, where the category is a variable, and
the scheme-level declarations are applications of those lemmas, elaborated at default
transparency. `CategoryTheory.sum_proj_comp_inj_of_hom_ext` and
`CategoryTheory.MonoidalClosed.ihomIsoOfDualBasis` exist for that reason: they take the
coordinates, the inclusions and the joint-epimorphy of the points as hypotheses, so that nothing
has to be rewritten on this side.

`MonoidalPreadditive` is what turns `∑ i, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F` into a statement about `F ⟶[C] Y`,
and it is not an instance on `ModuleSheaf S`:
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.Strict.monoidalPreadditiveRingSheaf` is a theorem ascribed at the strict
monoidal structure, supplied by `letI` in each proof that needs it. The statements themselves
need only `Preadditive`, for the zero morphism.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A2J](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A2J)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A2K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A2K)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory MonoidalCategory Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace
open Stacks.SheafOfModules

noncomputable section

universe v u

namespace CategoryTheory

/-- **A finite family of points whose coordinates are the Kronecker delta and which is jointly
epimorphic is a dual basis.** If `inj i : A ⟶ P` is jointly epimorphic and `proj j : P ⟶ A`
satisfies `inj i ≫ proj j = δ_{ij}`, then `∑ j, proj j ≫ inj j = 𝟙 P`, i.e. `P` is the biproduct
of copies of `A`. -/
lemma sum_proj_comp_inj_of_hom_ext {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [Preadditive C] {ι : Type*}
    [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] {A P : C} (inj : ι → (A ⟶ P))
    (hP : ∀ {N : C} {u v : P ⟶ N}, (∀ i, inj i ≫ u = inj i ≫ v) → u = v)
    (proj : ι → (P ⟶ A)) (hproj : ∀ i j, inj i ≫ proj j = if i = j then 𝟙 A else 0) :
    ∑ j, proj j ≫ inj j = 𝟙 P := by
  refine hP fun i => ?_
  have key : ∀ j : ι, inj i ≫ proj j ≫ inj j = if i = j then inj j else 0 := by
    intro j
    rw [← Category.assoc, hproj i j]
    by_cases hij : i = j
    · rw [ite_eq_left hij, ite_eq_left hij, Category.id_comp]
    · rw [ite_eq_right hij, ite_eq_right hij, Limits.zero_comp]
  rw [Preadditive.comp_sum]
  simp only [key]
  rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq Finset.univ i inj, Category.comp_id, ite_eq_left (Finset.mem_univ i)]

namespace MonoidalClosed

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] [MonoidalCategory C] [MonoidalClosed C]

/-- The coordinate of the internal hom attached to a point `e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F`: evaluate at `e`. -/
def ihomCoord {F : C} (e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F) (Y : C) : (ihom F).obj Y ⟶ Y :=
  (λ_ ((ihom F).obj Y)).inv ≫ (e ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (ihom.ev F).app Y

/-- The inclusion into the internal hom attached to a coordinate `p : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C`. -/
def ihomIncl {F : C} (p : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C) (Y : C) : Y ⟶ (ihom F).obj Y :=
  curry (p ▷ Y ≫ (λ_ Y).hom)

/-- The inclusion attached to `p` followed by the coordinate attached to `e` is the endomorphism
of `Y` given by whiskering the scalar `e ≫ p` with `Y`. -/
lemma ihomIncl_comp_ihomCoord {F : C} (p : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C) (e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F) (Y : C) :
    ihomIncl p Y ≫ ihomCoord e Y = (λ_ Y).inv ≫ ((e ≫ p) ▷ Y) ≫ (λ_ Y).hom := by
  rw [ihomCoord, ihomIncl, leftUnitor_inv_naturality_assoc, whisker_exchange_assoc,
    whiskerLeft_curry_ihom_ev_app, comp_whiskerRight]
  simp

/-- Precomposed with the left unitor, the coordinate attached to `e` is evaluation at `e`. -/
lemma leftUnitor_comp_ihomCoord {F : C} (e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F) (Y : C) :
    (λ_ ((ihom F).obj Y)).hom ≫ ihomCoord e Y
      = (e ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (ihom.ev F).app Y := by
  rw [ihomCoord, Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc]

/-- The uncurried form of the coordinate attached to `e` followed by the inclusion attached to
`p` is evaluation precomposed with the endomorphism `p ≫ e` of `F`. -/
lemma uncurry_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl {F : C} (e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F) (p : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C) (Y : C) :
    uncurry (ihomCoord e Y ≫ ihomIncl p Y)
      = ((p ≫ e) ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (ihom.ev F).app Y := by
  calc uncurry (ihomCoord e Y ≫ ihomIncl p Y)
      = (F ◁ ihomCoord e Y) ≫ (F ◁ ihomIncl p Y) ≫ (ihom.ev F).app Y := by
        rw [uncurry_eq, MonoidalCategory.whiskerLeft_comp, Category.assoc]
    _ = (F ◁ ihomCoord e Y) ≫ (p ▷ Y) ≫ (λ_ Y).hom := by
        rw [ihomIncl, whiskerLeft_curry_ihom_ev_app]
    _ = (p ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (𝟙_ C ◁ ihomCoord e Y) ≫ (λ_ Y).hom := by
        rw [whisker_exchange_assoc]
    _ = (p ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (λ_ ((ihom F).obj Y)).hom ≫ ihomCoord e Y := by
        simp
    _ = ((p ≫ e) ▷ (ihom F).obj Y) ≫ (ihom.ev F).app Y := by
        rw [leftUnitor_comp_ihomCoord, comp_whiskerRight, Category.assoc]

section Preadditive

variable [Preadditive C] [MonoidalPreadditive C]

/-- The coordinates and the inclusions of an internal hom are a system of matrix units: on the
diagonal of a dual basis the composite is the identity, off the diagonal it is zero. -/
lemma ihomIncl_comp_ihomCoord_ite {F : C} (p : F ⟶ 𝟙_ C) (e : 𝟙_ C ⟶ F) (Y : C) {P : Prop}
    [Decidable P] (h : e ≫ p = if P then 𝟙 (𝟙_ C) else 0) :
    ihomIncl p Y ≫ ihomCoord e Y = if P then 𝟙 Y else 0 := by
  rw [ihomIncl_comp_ihomCoord, h]
  by_cases hP : P
  · rw [ite_eq_left hP, ite_eq_left hP, MonoidalCategory.id_whiskerRight, Category.id_comp,
      Iso.inv_hom_id]
  · rw [ite_eq_right hP, ite_eq_right hP, MonoidalPreadditive.zero_whiskerRight, Limits.zero_comp,
      Limits.comp_zero]

/-- **A finite dual basis of `F` splits the internal hom out of `F` into its coordinates.** -/
lemma sum_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl {F : C} {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι)
    (e : ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ F)) (p : ι → (F ⟶ 𝟙_ C)) (htot : ∑ i ∈ s, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F) (Y : C) :
    ∑ i ∈ s, ihomCoord (e i) Y ≫ ihomIncl (p i) Y = 𝟙 ((ihom F).obj Y) := by
  apply uncurry_injective
  have h : uncurry (∑ i ∈ s, ihomCoord (e i) Y ≫ ihomIncl (p i) Y)
      = ∑ i ∈ s, uncurry (ihomCoord (e i) Y ≫ ihomIncl (p i) Y) := by
    simp only [uncurry_eq, whiskerLeft_sum, Preadditive.sum_comp]
  rw [h, uncurry_id_eq_ev]
  simp only [uncurry_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl]
  rw [← Preadditive.sum_comp, ← sum_whiskerRight, htot]
  simp

/-- **Morphisms out of an internal hom `F ⟶[C] Y` are determined by their composites with the
coordinate inclusions**, when `F` has a finite dual basis. -/
theorem hom_ext_of_dualBasis {F : C} {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι)
    (e : ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ F)) (p : ι → (F ⟶ 𝟙_ C)) (htot : ∑ i ∈ s, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F)
    {Y M : C} {θ θ' : (ihom F).obj Y ⟶ M}
    (h : ∀ i ∈ s, ihomIncl (p i) Y ≫ θ = ihomIncl (p i) Y ≫ θ') : θ = θ' := by
  rw [← Category.id_comp θ, ← Category.id_comp θ',
    ← sum_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl s e p htot Y, Preadditive.sum_comp, Preadditive.sum_comp]
  exact Finset.sum_congr rfl fun i hi => by
    rw [Category.assoc, Category.assoc, h i hi]

/-- **Morphisms out of an internal hom `F ⟶[C] Y` agreeing on all points are equal**, when `F`
has a finite dual basis and `Y` is generated by its points. -/
theorem hom_ext_of_curry' {F : C} {ι : Type*} (s : Finset ι)
    (e : ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ F)) (p : ι → (F ⟶ 𝟙_ C)) (htot : ∑ i ∈ s, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F)
    {Y M : C}
    (hY : ∀ {N : C} {u v : Y ⟶ N}, (∀ d : 𝟙_ C ⟶ Y, d ≫ u = d ≫ v) → u = v)
    {θ θ' : (ihom F).obj Y ⟶ M}
    (h : ∀ f : F ⟶ Y, curry' f ≫ θ = curry' f ≫ θ') : θ = θ' := by
  refine hom_ext_of_dualBasis s e p htot fun i _ => hY fun d => ?_
  rw [← Category.assoc, ← Category.assoc, ← curry'_uncurry' (d ≫ ihomIncl (p i) Y)]
  exact h _

/-- **An object with a matching family of points indexed by `ι × ι` is the internal endomorphism
object of an object with a dual basis indexed by `ι`.** The data is: a dual basis `e, p` of `F`
indexed by a finite type `ι`; an object `Q` with a jointly epimorphic family of points
`d : ι × ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ Q)` and "row" morphisms `row i : F ⟶ Q` with `e j ≫ row i = d (i, j)`; and a
morphism `hom : Q ⟶ F ⟶[C] F` carrying `d (i, j)` to the `(i, j)`-th matrix unit. -/
def ihomIsoOfDualBasis {F Q : C} {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι]
    (e : ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ F)) (p : ι → (F ⟶ 𝟙_ C)) (htot : ∑ i, p i ≫ e i = 𝟙 F)
    (hp : ∀ i j, e i ≫ p j = if i = j then 𝟙 (𝟙_ C) else 0)
    (d : ι × ι → (𝟙_ C ⟶ Q)) (row : ι → (F ⟶ Q)) (hrow : ∀ i j, e j ≫ row i = d (i, j))
    (hF : ∀ {N : C} {u v : F ⟶ N}, (∀ i, e i ≫ u = e i ≫ v) → u = v)
    (hQ : ∀ {N : C} {u v : Q ⟶ N}, (∀ k, d k ≫ u = d k ≫ v) → u = v)
    (hom : Q ⟶ (ihom F).obj F)
    (hhom : ∀ i j, d (i, j) ≫ hom = e j ≫ ihomIncl (p i) F) :
    Q ≅ (ihom F).obj F where
  hom := hom
  inv := ∑ i, ihomCoord (e i) F ≫ row i
  hom_inv_id := by
    refine hQ fun k => ?_
    obtain ⟨a, b⟩ := k
    have key : ∀ m : ι, d (a, b) ≫ hom ≫ ihomCoord (e m) F ≫ row m
        = if m = a then d (a, b) else 0 := by
      intro m
      rw [← Category.assoc (d (a, b)), hhom a b, Category.assoc,
        ← Category.assoc (ihomIncl (p a) F), ihomIncl_comp_ihomCoord_ite _ _ _ (hp m a)]
      by_cases hm : m = a
      · rw [ite_eq_left hm, ite_eq_left hm, Category.id_comp, hm, hrow a b]
      · rw [ite_eq_right hm, ite_eq_right hm, Limits.zero_comp, Limits.comp_zero]
    rw [Preadditive.comp_sum, Preadditive.comp_sum]
    simp only [key]
    rw [Finset.sum_ite_eq' Finset.univ a (fun _ => d (a, b)), Category.comp_id,
      ite_eq_left (Finset.mem_univ a)]
  inv_hom_id := by
    have hrowhom : ∀ i, row i ≫ hom = ihomIncl (p i) F := fun i =>
      hF fun j => by rw [← Category.assoc, hrow i j, hhom i j]
    rw [Preadditive.sum_comp]
    simp only [Category.assoc, hrowhom]
    exact sum_ihomCoord_comp_ihomIncl Finset.univ e p htot F

end Preadditive

end MonoidalClosed

end CategoryTheory

namespace Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme

variable {S : Scheme.{u}}

/-- The free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules on a type `I`, at the spelling of this namespace. -/
abbrev freeModule (S : Scheme.{u}) (I : Type u) : ModuleSheaf S :=
  SheafOfModules.free (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) I

/-- The unit of the tensor product of sheaves of `𝒪_S`-modules is `𝒪_S`. -/
lemma unit_eq_tensorUnit (S : Scheme.{u}) :
    SheafOfModules.unit (Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) = 𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S) := rfl

/-- The `i`-th tautological point of the free sheaf of modules on `I`. -/
abbrev freeInj {I : Type u} (i : I) : 𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S) ⟶ freeModule S I :=
  SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) i

/-- The `j`-th coordinate of the free sheaf of modules on a type with decidable equality. -/
def freeProj {I : Type u} [DecidableEq I] (j : I) : freeModule S I ⟶ 𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S) :=
  Cofan.IsColimit.desc (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) I)
    (fun i => if i = j then 𝟙 (𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S)) else 0)

/-- The `j`-th coordinate of the `i`-th tautological point is the Kronecker delta `δ_{ij}`. -/
@[simp]
lemma freeInj_comp_freeProj {I : Type u} [DecidableEq I] (i j : I) :
    freeInj (S := S) i ≫ freeProj j = if i = j then 𝟙 (𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S)) else 0 :=
  Cofan.IsColimit.fac (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) I)
    (fun i => if i = j then 𝟙 (𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S)) else 0) i

/-- Two morphisms out of a free sheaf of modules agreeing on every tautological point are
equal. -/
lemma freeModule_hom_ext_inj {I : Type u} {N : ModuleSheaf S} {u v : freeModule S I ⟶ N}
    (h : ∀ i : I, freeInj (S := S) i ≫ u = freeInj i ≫ v) : u = v :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.FreeSheafification.free_hom_ext (Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) h

/-- Two morphisms out of a free sheaf of modules agreeing on every point are equal. -/
lemma freeModule_hom_ext {I : Type u} {N : ModuleSheaf S} {u v : freeModule S I ⟶ N}
    (h : ∀ d : 𝟙_ (ModuleSheaf S) ⟶ freeModule S I, d ≫ u = d ≫ v) : u = v :=
  freeModule_hom_ext_inj fun i => h (freeInj i)

/-- **The tautological points and coordinates are a dual basis of a finite free sheaf of
`𝒪_S`-modules.** -/
lemma sum_freeProj_comp_freeInj {I : Type u} [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I] :
    ∑ j : I, freeProj (S := S) j ≫ freeInj j = 𝟙 (freeModule S I) :=
  CategoryTheory.sum_proj_comp_inj_of_hom_ext (fun i => freeInj (S := S) i)
    (fun hd => freeModule_hom_ext_inj hd) (fun j => freeProj j) freeInj_comp_freeProj

/-- **Two morphisms out of the endomorphism algebra of a finite free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules
which agree on all points are equal.** -/
theorem endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext {I : Type u} [Finite I] {M : ModuleSheaf S}
    {θ θ' : (endAlgebra (freeModule S I)).X ⟶ M}
    (h : ∀ f : freeModule S I ⟶ freeModule S I,
      MonoidalClosed.curry' f ≫ θ = MonoidalClosed.curry' f ≫ θ') :
    θ = θ' := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite I
  let : MonoidalPreadditive (ModuleSheaf S) := Strict.monoidalPreadditiveRingSheaf S.sheaf
  exact MonoidalClosed.hom_ext_of_curry' Finset.univ (fun i => freeInj (S := S) i)
    (fun j => freeProj j) sum_freeProj_comp_freeInj
    (fun hd => freeModule_hom_ext hd) h

/-- **Two morphisms of sheaves of algebras out of the endomorphism algebra of a finite free sheaf
of `𝒪_S`-modules which agree on all points are equal.** -/
theorem endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext' {I : Type u} [Finite I] {A : AlgebraSheaf S}
    {θ θ' : endAlgebra (freeModule S I) ⟶ A}
    (h : ∀ f : freeModule S I ⟶ freeModule S I,
      MonoidalClosed.curry' f ≫ θ.hom = MonoidalClosed.curry' f ≫ θ'.hom) :
    θ = θ' :=
  Mon.Hom.ext (endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext h)

/-- **A morphism of sheaves of algebras out of `End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` is determined by the map it
induces on endomorphisms**, for a finite index type `I`. -/
theorem eq_of_pointMap_eq {I : Type u} [Finite I] {E : ModuleSheaf S}
    {θ θ' : endAlgebra (freeModule S I) ⟶ endAlgebra E}
    (h : ∀ f : freeModule S I ⟶ freeModule S I,
      MonoidalClosed.pointMap θ f = MonoidalClosed.pointMap θ' f) :
    θ = θ' := by
  refine endAlgebra_freeModule_hom_ext' fun f => ?_
  rw [← MonoidalClosed.curry'_pointMap θ f, ← MonoidalClosed.curry'_pointMap θ' f, h f]

/-! ### The endomorphism algebra of a finite free sheaf of modules is free -/

/-- The comparison `𝒪_S^{(I × I)} ⟶ End(𝒪_S^{(I)})`: the generator indexed by `(i, j)` goes to
the elementary endomorphism which reads off the `i`-th coordinate and writes it in the `j`-th
place. -/
def freeProdToEndAlgebra {I : Type u} [DecidableEq I] :
    freeModule S (I × I) ⟶ (endAlgebra (freeModule S I)).X :=
  Cofan.IsColimit.desc
    (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) (I × I))
    (fun k => freeInj (S := S) k.2 ≫
      MonoidalClosed.ihomIncl (freeProj (S := S) k.1) (freeModule S I))

/-- The comparison `freeProdToEndAlgebra` sends the generator indexed by `(i, j)` to the
elementary endomorphism which reads off the `i`-th coordinate and writes it in the `j`-th
place. -/
@[simp]
lemma freeInj_comp_freeProdToEndAlgebra {I : Type u} [DecidableEq I] (i j : I) :
    freeInj (S := S) (i, j) ≫ freeProdToEndAlgebra
      = freeInj (S := S) j ≫
        MonoidalClosed.ihomIncl (freeProj (S := S) i) (freeModule S I) :=
  Cofan.IsColimit.fac
    (SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) (I × I))
    (fun k => freeInj (S := S) k.2 ≫
      MonoidalClosed.ihomIncl (freeProj (S := S) k.1) (freeModule S I)) (i, j)

/-- **The endomorphism algebra sheaf of a finite free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules is itself a finite
free sheaf of `𝒪_S`-modules**: `𝒪_S^{(I × I)} ≅ End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` as sheaves of modules, the
isomorphism being the system of matrix units. -/
def freeProdIsoEndAlgebra (S : Scheme.{u}) (I : Type u) [Fintype I] [DecidableEq I] :
    freeModule S (I × I) ≅ (endAlgebra (freeModule S I)).X :=
  letI : MonoidalPreadditive (ModuleSheaf S) := Strict.monoidalPreadditiveRingSheaf S.sheaf
  MonoidalClosed.ihomIsoOfDualBasis (fun i => freeInj (S := S) i) (fun j => freeProj j)
    sum_freeProj_comp_freeInj freeInj_comp_freeProj (fun k => freeInj (S := S) k)
    (fun i => SheafOfModules.freeMap (R := Tensor.ringSheaf S.sheaf) (fun j => (i, j)))
    (fun i j => SheafOfModules.ιFree_freeMap (fun j => (i, j)) j)
    (fun hd => freeModule_hom_ext_inj hd) (fun hd => freeModule_hom_ext_inj hd)
    freeProdToEndAlgebra freeInj_comp_freeProdToEndAlgebra

/-- **`End(𝒪_S^{(I)})` is free of rank the square of the cardinality of `I`** for a finite index
type, stated with `Nonempty` because the isomorphism depends on an enumeration of `I`. -/
theorem nonempty_iso_freeProd_endAlgebra (S : Scheme.{u}) (I : Type u) [Finite I] :
    Nonempty ((endAlgebra (freeModule S I)).X ≅ freeModule S (I × I)) := by
  classical
  let := Fintype.ofFinite I
  exact ⟨(freeProdIsoEndAlgebra S I).symm⟩

end Stacks.EtaleCohomology.BrauerScheme

